### Approval chains API v1. Every request needs the access token from the sign in request below.
### Select the "local" environment (http/http-client.env.json). Run requests top to bottom.

### Sign in (put login and password in http/http-client.private.env.json, which is git-ignored)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "login": "{{login}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Seeded: chain 1 is the default; department ids 2 Administratives, 3 Accounting, 4 Quality Check.

### List chains (default first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Get the default chain
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Edit the default chain: ordered approving departments
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Default",
  "description": "Company wide",
  "departmentIds": [3, 4, 2]
}

### Which chain does catalog 1000 follow? (own chain, else the default)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/for-catalog/1000
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Give catalog 1000 its own chain (409 if it already has one)
# @name create
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Premium bags",
  "catalogId": 1000,
  "departmentIds": [3, 4, 2]
}

### Deactivate the catalog chain (the catalog follows the default meanwhile; 409 for the default chain)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Activate it again
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### The default chain cannot be deactivated (409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/1/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Delete the catalog chain (the catalog goes back to the default)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/{{create.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### The default chain cannot be deleted (409)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Without an acting user changes return 401
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Default", "departmentIds": [4] }

### Unknown id returns 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Accept: application/json
